{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEightTelescope","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEightTelescope","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.newtonLadder_lam_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.newtonLadder_lam_split","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightTelescope.lean#L143-L152","doc":"The tower specialization `x = q^N`: the colored-Jones ladder element,\ncleared, is the split product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.newtonLadder_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.newtonLadder_split","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightTelescope.lean#L121-L141","doc":"**The cleared Newton ladder (division-free)**: multiplying the ladder\nelement at `x + x⁻¹` by the product of the per-factor denominators\nyields the split product `A(k)·B(k)`.  Generic in `x ≠ 0` — the tower\ncase is `x = q^N` (`newtonLadder_lam_split`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.ladder_factor_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.ladder_factor_split","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightTelescope.lean#L111-L119","doc":"**Per-factor split**: clearing the single denominator `x·q^{j+1}` of a\nladder factor at `x + x⁻¹` splits it into the two linear halves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingB_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingB_shift","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightTelescope.lean#L89-L102","doc":"**Color shift for `B` (division-free)**: shifting `x → q·x` re-indexes\nthe nodes one step up, so prepending the lowest factor recovers the\nunshifted product one rung higher:\n`(x·q − 1) · B_{qx}(k) = B_x(k+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingA_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingA_shift","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightTelescope.lean#L74-L87","doc":"**Color shift for `A` (division-free)**: shifting `x → q·x` (one color\nup, `N → N+1`) and one rung up factors as\n`A_{qx}(k+1) = q^{k+1} · (x − 1) · A_x(k)` — the `(x − 1)` is the\n`(1 − 1/x)`-numerator of the certificate ratio `r₁`, cleared. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingB_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingB_succ","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightTelescope.lean#L70-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingA_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingA_succ","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightTelescope.lean#L66-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingB_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingB_zero","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightTelescope.lean#L63-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingA_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingA_zero","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightTelescope.lean#L60-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingB","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightTelescope.lean#L55-L58","doc":"Second split half: `B(k) = ∏_{j<k} (x·q^{j+1} − 1)` — pole-free on the\ntower (at `x = q^N` it vanishes only at roots of unity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.risingA","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEightTelescope.lean#L50-L53","doc":"First split half: `A(k) = ∏_{j<k} (x − q^{j+1})` — carries the\ntermination zeros (`x = q^N` kills it at `k ≥ N`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}